<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:40:04Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22c0a1275f95a307402586250fb9638cc459ccc738c4d14141c9644e295539ef</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ec7fa1f87658d6675e55999608af12b74b0bc702998f228205997afd1ebc0535</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:28Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T14:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan's road to elections remains uncertain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2851cb5f6e5a060738ce541d7ce9dd54acf8c1be928da509cea19c020bb4656a</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442--6016ef79f3a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-s-road-to-elections-remains-uncertain/a-79563442?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan's first general election is set for December 22. Insecurity, political tensions and failure to begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether the poll can be held credibly.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Golden Week reveals cautious consumer spending despite travel surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72be2be1c5289a9816fc2a76813b33548f0aebe3389aa745a87183940347b635</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:39:34Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254--362469c231fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chinese visitors are returning from trips after the 13-day Golden Week holiday. Their subdued spending has raised fresh questions about domestic demand in the world's second-largest economy.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7a33b1a5ef29546b64f8c7a2e2088cab2ff335a8866a111188d698366d17089</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim strikes on Aden, Riyadh airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1fbd9f52bd2797308eb7cb0dbe247a2c435484b3e581e37228b46f9442dcf8</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:40:04Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321--0245466ede4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aden International Airport came under attack as Yemen's war intensified, with the Houthis targeting key transport hubs. Around 200,000 people have been displaced by the fighting between government forces and the Houthis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2735242b9aebdd6338d819f82f350a22e38d29f4743744c69f8a81ea489f64d</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad84b73638efa89d407ea4adb3306188db14cabc06f830c7a2ee8a693b0ce162</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc75af03942e6447cba3f36ddedfbc00a2f5bc7b04a5bc0bf7334aeadbbace0a</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:621ce36dd8e0c4f735f0deb001e10e92177302653768caece06f616166f0400e</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As more Iranian women reject hijab rules, regime looks at new ways to force compliance</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:02a849a385948368b999b4039caf57a1b8988c69f420ee9fa2a47ac713a477f9</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962--9c09f80416a6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-more-iranian-women-reject-hijab-rules-regime-looks-at-new-ways-to-force-compliance/a-79564962?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As more women in Iran reject rules on wearing hijab headscarves, hardliners are shifting focus from "morality police" street enforcement towards social pressure in workplaces, services and businesses.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray war may spill over to Eritrea — helped by Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's rhetoric</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40166d81d63e9635adcf31982ea6548781087c7e49930eaef3c9947020f23dc5</id><updated>2026-10-07T15:38:27Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957--f357fb8ada5f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tigray-war-may-spill-over-to-eritrea-helped-by-prime-minister-abiy-ahmed-s-rhetoric/a-79562957?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ethiopia's Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed is consolidating power, but he must contend with a regional alliance opposing him and a Tigray conflict that could spill over into Eritrea.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
